{"text": "Calumet Avenue Tax Service\n5512 Merrill Road, Suite B · Jacksonville, FL 32277 · (904) 555-0118\n\nPaid Preparer Due Diligence Checklist — Tax Year 2025\n\nPreparer: Ines Quaresma-Lott, EA | PTIN: P01844720 | Client file: CA-25-0611 | Interview: 02/11/2026\n\nTaxpayer\n\nName\n\nAdaeze N. Nkemelu (return will show NKEMELU, ADAEZE N)\n\nSSN\n\n353-98-2165\n\nDate of birth\n\n14 Oct 1991\n\nAddress\n\n7741 Lone Star Rd, Unit 208, Jacksonville, FL 32211-4406\n\nPhone / email\n\n904 555 0163 / adaeze.nkemelu@postbox.example\n\nFiling status\n\nHead of Household (see Q3 notes — spouse lived apart all of 2025)\n\nIP PIN\n\n407715 (Notice CP09 not relevant; PIN letter seen and copied)\n\nQualifying Children\n\nName\tSSN\tBorn\tRelationship\tMonths lived with taxpayer\tGrade / care\n\nChidera Nkemelu\t797-11-1006\t05/22/2016\tdaughter\t12\t4th grade, Ribault Bend Elementary\n\nKelechi Nkemelu\t763 96 8188\t2019-09-03\tson\t12\tKindergarten since Aug. 11; before that Mulberry Lane Child Development Center\n\nKnowledge questions and answers\n\nQ1. Income. One Form W-2 from Dunes Edge Home Care, LLC (EIN 59-3317746): Box 1 wages $27,914.62, federal withholding $1,106.00. No self-employment. She confirmed she did not braid hair for pay in 2025 (she did in 2023; that return was Self-prepared).\n\nQ2. Residency of children. Both children lived with her all 12 months at the Lone Star Rd apartment. Proof retained: lease naming all three (Jan 1 – Dec 31, 2025); Ribault Bend enrollment letter dated 1/29/2026 signed by the registrar; Arlington Shores Pediatrics immunization record for Kelechi showing the same address.\n\nQ3. Marital status / HOH. Married to Obinna Nkemelu; he moved out November 2024 and lives with a cousin in Orange Park. No joint return. Obinna has no SSN and is not authorized to work; his ITIN is 9XX-78-4416 (expired, Form W-7 renewal not filed). He paid nothing toward rent. She paid rent of $1,385/mo and all utilities; I added it up and she paid more than half the cost of the home. Considered-unmarried test met, so HOH not MFS.\n\nQ4. Could anyone else claim the children? Her mother, Patience Eze, stayed with them June–August on a visitor visa and is not a taxpayer. Mrs. Eze is not claiming anyone. Obinna will not file.\n\nQ5. Prior disallowance. None. Form 8862 not required.\n\nCredits Claimed\n\nCredit\tAmount\tNotes\n\nEITC (Schedule EIC, 2 children)\t$6,418\tearned income and AGI both $27,914.62 rounded\n\nCTC / ACTC\t$4,000.00\tboth children have SSNs valid for work\n\nChild and Dependent Care Credit (Form 2441)\t$600\tpaid Mulberry Lane $3,150 Jan–Aug for Kelechi; provider EIN 47-2095513\n\nRefund\n\nFederal refund $10,912. Direct deposit to Sabal Coast Community Credit Union, Savings, Routing 063855302, account 70044182265. Fee of $240.00 paid by debit card at pickup; no refund transfer product.\n\nPreparer's notes\n\nClient receives SNAP and asked whether the refund counts against it; told her to ask her caseworker and gave her Pub. 4687 only as my own reference list. Chidera has an IEP for a speech delay — not relevant to any credit but Ms. Nkemelu mentioned it when explaining the school letter. Explained the penalty rules to her in plain words (IRC § 6695(g); Treas. Reg. § 1.6695-2). Documents Retained: copies in the portal folder https://portal.calumettax.example/clients/CA-25-0611/8867. Form 8867 completed and attached to Form 1040. — IQL, 2/12/26", "kind": "Web page", "detail": "530 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Adaeze N. Nkemelu", "Ines Quaresma-Lott", "Obinna Nkemelu", "Chidera Nkemelu", "Kelechi Nkemelu", "Patience Eze", "Obinna", "Chidera", "Kelechi", "Ms. Nkemelu"], "companies": ["Calumet Avenue Tax Service", "Dunes Edge Home Care, LLC", "Arlington Shores Pediatrics", "Mulberry Lane"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Jacksonville", "FL", "Ribault Bend Elementary", "Arlington Shores Pediatrics", "Lone Star Rd", "Orange Park", "Sabal Coast Community Credit Union", "Mulberry Lane"], "health": ["